SGO_COMMENTARY.push({"id":"julius-africanus","author":"Julius Africanus","work":"Julius Africanus The Epistle to Aristides; The Epistle to Aristides, I; Fragment","translator":"Public-domain English translations (Ante-Nicene and Nicene & Post-Nicene Fathers, Library of the Fathers, Newman's Catena Aurea and others)","lang":"en","license":"Public Domain","source":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Commentaries-Database (Julius Africanus/)","versification":"kjv","tradition":"early","notes":{"GEN.6.1-4":["When men multiplied on the earth, the angels of heaven came together with the daughters of men. In some copies I found \"the sons of God.\" What is meant by the Spirit, in my opinion, is that the descendants of Seth are called the sons of God on account of the righteous men and patriarchs who have sprung from him, even down to the Saviour Himself; but that the descendants of Cain are named the seed of men, as having nothing divine in them, on account of the wickedness of their race and the inequality of their nature, being a mixed people, and having stirred the indignation of God. But if it is thought that these refer to angels, we must take them to be those who deal with magic and jugglery, who taught the women the motions of the stars and the knowledge of things celestial, by whose power they conceived the giants as their children, by whom wickedness came to its height on the earth, until God decreed that the whole race of the living should perish in their impiety by the deluge.\n— Fragment 2"],"LUK.3.23":["But if, with Luke, we reckon them from Nathan the son of David, in like manner the third from the end is Mel chi, whose son was Heli the father of Joseph. For Joseph was the son of Hell, the son of Mel chi.\n— Julius Africanus The Epistle to Aristides"],"1CO.15.12":["Nor shall an assertion of this kind prevail in the Church of Christ against the exact truth, so as that a lie should be contrived for the praise and glory of Christ. For who does not know that most holy word of the apostle also, who, when he was preaching and proclaiming the resurrection of our Saviour, and confidently affirming the truth, said with great fear, \"If any say that Christ is not risen, and we assert and have believed this, and both hope for and preach that very thing, we are false witnesses of God, in alleging that He raised up Christ, whom He raised not up?\" And if he who glorifies God the Father is thus afraid lest he should seem a false witness in narrating a marvellous fact, how should not he be justly afraid, who tries to establish the truth by a false statement, preparing an untrue opinion?\n— The Epistle to Aristides, I"],"HEB.7.14":["And they ought not indeed to have been ignorant that both orders of the ancestors enumerated are the generation of David, the royal tribe of Juda.\n— Julius Africanus The Epistle to Aristides"]}});
